'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

--- RECORDING: EVENT TRIGGER VARIABLE ---
RNL_flight_recording (default: false)

Turns true when recording starts. Perfect for creating highly synchronized scenes!
Use this variable in editor triggers (Condition: RNL_flight_recording) to:
- Simultaneously start another playback of a different vehicle at the exact same moment.
- Trigger custom scripts, ambient effects, or infantry waypoints the second you press record.

--- RHS AIRCRAFT ---
Please use empty vehicles in the editor to prevent ejection seat bugs at mission start.

--- IMPORTANT NOTE: TROOP UNLOADING & RAPPELLING --
The system will automatically pause the playback whenever troops are being unloaded on the ground 
or via rappelling (fast-roping).

Seamless Recording: 
You can simply place the respective marker during your recording session and continue flying 
to carry on with your recording.

Visual Tip for Realism: 
Even though you can technically fly away immediately, it is highly recommended to briefly touch down 
(for ground unloading) or hold a steady hover (for rappelling) for a brief moment right when 
placing the marker. 

This ensures the final playback animation looks 
clean, realistic, and professional!

Summary: 
The script handles the heavy lifting and pauses the timeline for you automatically, but a short, 
deliberate pause on your end during the recording makes the troop insertion look absolutely perfect 
in-game!

- - - - INFO END - - - - - - - - INFO END - - - - - - - - INFO END - - - - - - - - INFO END - - - -';





